// CACHE: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits | owner=CodeEditorLand | repo=Mountain | per_page=5 | page=16 → GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits.RESPONSE.map(Author,Date,File,Message,SHA)
{
	"Set": [
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-10T20:51:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1505,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(FSSRV): add empty-path guard + URI strip to Stat, ReadDirectory, ReadFile\n\nFileSystem.Stat and FileSystem.ReadDirectory had no empty-path guard,\nunlike FileSystem.ReadFile which already had one (added in the\n`LooksLike404` classifier batch). An extension passing an empty string\nto `vscode.workspace.fs.stat` or `readDirectory` (probe-on-activate\npattern) hit PathBuf::from(\"\") which:\n  - On Stat: reached the OS with an empty path and returned a\n    platform-dependent error string that did NOT match any of the eight\n    known \"not found\" patterns in MountainVinegRPCService, so the\n    LooksLike404 guard logged it at grpc/error and incremented the\n    circuit-breaker counter.\n  - On ReadDirectory: same failure path, plus PathSecurity could emit\n    \"path outside workspace\" which was previously only guarded on the\n    ReadFile arm.\n\nFix: mirror the ReadFile guard verbatim on both Stat and ReadDirectory.\nThe \"resource not found\" suffix in the error string is the canonical\nkey the LooksLike404 classifier matches on, so these errors now\ndowngrade to grpc-verbose and use code -32004 like ReadFile does.\n\nStripFileUriScheme is already called on the path_str in both arms;\nthis commit makes that call consistent - the strip was missing on\nReadDirectory before the empty-path branch was added, leaving\nfile:///absolute/path inputs reaching the OS with the scheme intact\nand 404-ing with a literal \"file:\" prefix in the error.",
			"SHA": "701563143aa3d55befc5f0b1adc173057a1dc30c"
		},
